# RPC

RPC owns the native server: service declarations, handlers, call scopes, transport limits, admission, deadlines, and shutdown. Generated calls and client transport lifecycle remain canonical under <GuideRef slug="clients/native/rpc">native RPC clients</GuideRef> and are not duplicated here.

## Choose a server task

| Task | Guide |
|---|---|
| declare a service, add unary or streaming operations, and inject call dependencies | <GuideRef slug="rpc/server">RPC services</GuideRef> |
| configure admission, limits, deadlines, connection handling, and graceful shutdown | <GuideRef slug="rpc/server/policies">Server policies</GuideRef> |

## Shared prerequisites

Start with an application using the `daemon` feature and a configured endpoint. Use <GuideRef slug="framework/application/lifecycle">application lifecycle</GuideRef> for process resources that surround the RPC runtime rather than one call.
